{"type": "step", "node_id": 23, "parent_node_id": 22, "role": "assistant", "content": "## Solution\n\n**Answer-leak check:** The problem statement contains only the definition of $S(n)$ and the request to evaluate $S(10)$. No solution, hint, or answer is leaked.\n\n---\n\n### Closed form for $S(n)$\n\nLet\n$$T(n)=\\sum_{k=0}^{n}(-1)^{k}(n+k)!(n-k)!,\\qquad S(n)=T(n)-(n!)^{2}.$$\n\nUsing $\\binom{2n}{n+k}=\\dfrac{(2n)!}{(n+k)!(n-k)!}$, i.e. $(n+k)!(n-k)!=\\dfrac{(2n)!}{\\binom{2n}{n+k}}$, and setting $j=n+k$:\n\n$$T(n)=(2n)!\\,(-1)^{n}\\sum_{j=n}^{2n}\\frac{(-1)^{j}}{\\binom{2n}{j}}=(2n)!\\,(-1)^{n}\\,U,\\quad U:=\\sum_{j=n}^{2n}\\frac{(-1)^{j}}{\\binom{2n}{j}}.$$\n\n**Evaluating the full alternating sum.** Using $\\dfrac{1}{\\binom{n}{k}}=(n+1)\\displaystyle\\int_{0}^{1}t^{k}(1-t)^{n-k}\\,dt$,\n\n$$\\sum_{k=0}^{n}\\frac{(-1)^{k}}{\\binom{n}{k}}=(n+1)\\int_{0}^{1}\\sum_{k=0}^{n}(1-t)^{n-k}(-t)^{k}\\,dt=(n+1)\\int_{0}^{1}\\!\\bigl[(1-t)^{n+1}-(-t)^{n+1}\\bigr]\\,dt$$\n\n$$=\\frac{n+1}{n+2}\\bigl(1-(-1)^{n+1}\\bigr)=\\frac{n+1}{n+2}\\bigl(1+(-1)^{n}\\bigr).$$\n\nFor $n\\to 2n$ (even), this gives\n$$A:=\\sum_{j=0}^{2n}\\frac{(-1)^{j}}{\\binom{2n}{j}}=\\frac{2n+1}{2n+2}\\cdot 2=\\frac{2n+1}{n+1}.$$\n\n**Relating $U$ to $A$.** By symmetry $\\binom{2n}{j}=\\binom{2n}{2n-j}$ and $(-1)^{2n-j}=(-1)^{j}$, so $\\sum_{j=0}^{n-1}=\\sum_{j=n+1}^{2n}$. Hence\n$$A=2\\sum_{j=0}^{n-1}\\frac{(-1)^{j}}{\\binom{2n}{j}}+\\frac{(-1)^{n}}{\\binom{2n}{n}},\\qquad U=\\frac{(-1)^{n}}{\\binom{2n}{n}}+\\sum_{j=0}^{n-1}\\frac{(-1)^{j}}{\\binom{2n}{j}}=\\frac{A+(-1)^{n}/\\binom{2n}{n}}{2}.$$\n\nTherefore\n$$T(n)=(2n)!\\,(-1)^{n}\\cdot\\frac{A+(-1)^{n}/\\binom{2n}{n}}{2}=\\frac{(2n)!\\,(-1)^{n}(2n+1)}{2(n+1)}+\\frac{(n!)^{2}}{2},$$\n\nand\n$$\\boxed{S(n)=\\frac{(-1)^{n}(2n)!(2n+1)}{2(n+1)}-\\frac{(n!)^{2}}{2}}.$$\n\n**Verification on small cases.** $S(1)=-2$, $S(2)=18$, $S(3)=-648$ — all match direct computation.\n\n### Evaluating $S(10)$\n\nWith $n=10$ (so $(-1)^{10}=1$):\n$$S(10)=\\frac{20!\\cdot